## Summary of Private-Vault Batch Move, Drag-and-Drop, and Single-Item Move Implementation

Based on my thorough analysis of the cipher-box codebase, here is the complete picture:

---

### **1. PRIVATE-VAULT SINGLE-ITEM MOVE PATH**

**Files & Key Lines:**
- **MoveDialog.tsx** (lines 162–329): The dialog component that handles both single and batch moves
  - Lines 20-21: Props support both `item` (single) and `items` (batch)
  - Lines 174-179: Resolves items array (batch takes precedence)
  - Line 181: `isBatch` flag determines title/label formatting

- **useFileBrowserActions.ts** (lines 520–532):
  ```typescript
  const handleMoveConfirm = useCallback(
    async (destinationFolderId: string) => {
      const item = moveDialog.item;
      if (!item) return;
      try {
        await moveItem(item.id, item.type, currentFolderId, destinationFolderId);
        closeMoveDialog();
      } catch (err) {
        logger.error('[FileBrowser] Move failed:', err);
      }
    },
    [moveDialog.item, moveItem, currentFolderId, closeMoveDialog]
  );
  ```
  - Calls `moveItem()` from `useFolderMutations`

- **FileBrowser.tsx** (lines 276–283):
  ```typescript
  <MoveDialog
    open={actions.moveDialog.open}
    onClose={actions.closeMoveDialog}
    onConfirm={actions.handleMoveConfirm}
    item={actions.moveDialog.item}
    currentFolderId={currentFolderId}
    isLoading={isOperating}
  />
  ```
  - Single-item move dialog wiring

- **useFolderMutations.ts** (lines 195–234):
  ```typescript
  const handleMove = useCallback(
    async (
      itemId: string,
      itemType: 'file' | 'folder',
      sourceParentId: string,
      destParentId: string
    ): Promise<void> => {
      setState({ isLoading: true, error: null });
      try {
        const sourceFolder = getParentFolder(sourceParentId);
        const destFolder = getParentFolder(destParentId);
        if (!sourceFolder || !destFolder) {
          throw new Error('Source or destination folder not found');
        }

        const client = getSdkClient();
        await client.moveItem(sourceFolder.ipnsName, destFolder.ipnsName, itemId);
        // ... updates folder parentId for moved folders ...
        setState({ isLoading: false, error: null });
      } catch (err) {
        // ... error handling ...
      }
    },
    []
  );
  ```
  - Calls **SDK `client.moveItem(sourceIpnsName, destIpnsName, itemId)`**

---

### **2. PRIVATE-VAULT BATCH MOVE IMPLEMENTATION**

**Multi-Selection State Holder:**
- **useFileBrowserActions.ts** (lines 218–234):
  ```typescript
  const [selectedIds, setSelectedIds] = useState<Set<string>>(new Set());
  const lastSelectedIdRef = useRef<string | null>(null);
  // ...
  const selectedItems = useMemo(
    () => children.filter((c) => selectedIds.has(c.id)),
    [children, selectedIds]
  );
  const multiSelectActive = selectedIds.size > 0;
  ```
  - Holds selected item IDs in a Set
  - `selectedItems` derived via useMemo
  - `multiSelectActive` flag for UI

**Batch Move Dialog State:**
- **useFileBrowserActions.ts** (lines 262–265):
  ```typescript
  const [batchMoveDialog, setBatchMoveDialog] = useState<{
    open: boolean;
    items: FolderChild[];
  }>({ open: false, items: [] });
  ```

**Batch Move Handler:**
- **useFileBrowserActions.ts** (lines 430–433):
  ```typescript
  const handleBatchMoveClick = useCallback(() => {
    if (selectedItems.length === 0) return;
    setBatchMoveDialog({ open: true, items: [...selectedItems] });
  }, [selectedItems]);
  ```
  - Triggered by SelectionActionBar (line 211: `onMove={actions.handleBatchMoveClick}`)

**Batch Move Confirmation:**
- **useFileBrowserActions.ts** (lines 468–485):
  ```typescript
  const handleBatchMoveConfirm = useCallback(
    async (destinationFolderId: string) => {
      const items = batchMoveDialog.items;
      if (items.length === 0) return;
      try {
        await moveItems(
          items.map((i) => ({ id: i.id, type: i.type })),
          currentFolderId,
          destinationFolderId
        );
        setBatchMoveDialog({ open: false, items: [] });
        clearSelection();
      } catch (err) {
        logger.error('[FileBrowser] Batch move failed:', err);
      }
    },
    [batchMoveDialog.items, moveItems, currentFolderId, clearSelection]
  );
  ```
  - Calls `moveItems()` from `useFolderMutations`

**Batch Move Dialog (2nd Instance):**
- **FileBrowser.tsx** (lines 375–383):
  ```typescript
  <MoveDialog
    open={actions.batchMoveDialog.open}
    onClose={actions.closeBatchMoveDialog}
    onConfirm={actions.handleBatchMoveConfirm}
    item={null}
    items={actions.batchMoveDialog.items}
    currentFolderId={currentFolderId}
    isLoading={isOperating}
  />
  ```
  - `item={null}` for batch, `items={...}` populated
  - MoveDialog.tsx line 176 handles batch label/title

**SDK Batch Move Call:**
- **useFolderMutations.ts** (lines 245–311):
  ```typescript
  const handleMoveItems = useCallback(
    async (
      items: Array<{ id: string; type: 'file' | 'folder' }>,
      sourceParentId: string,
      destParentId: string
    ): Promise<void> => {
      setState({ isLoading: true, error: null });
      try {
        const sourceFolder = getParentFolder(sourceParentId);
        const destFolder = getParentFolder(destParentId);
        if (!sourceFolder || !destFolder) {
          throw new Error('Source or destination folder not found');
        }

        // Validate batch move preconditions (lines 259-288)
        const folders = useFolderStore.getState().folders;
        const itemIds = new Set(items.map((i) => i.id));

        for (const item of items) {
          if (item.type === 'folder') {
            if (isDescendantOf(destFolder.id, item.id, folders)) {
              throw new Error(`Cannot move folder into itself or its subfolder`);
            }
            const destDepth = getDepth(destFolder.id, folders);
            const subtreeDepth = calculateSubtreeDepth(item.id, folders);
            if (destDepth + 1 + subtreeDepth > MAX_FOLDER_DEPTH) {
              throw new Error(
                `Cannot move: would exceed maximum folder depth of ${MAX_FOLDER_DEPTH}`
              );
            }
          }
        }

        // Name collision check (lines 281-288)
        const movedChildren = sourceFolder.children.filter((c) => itemIds.has(c.id));
        for (const child of movedChildren) {
          const nameExists = destFolder.children.some((c) => c.name === child.name);
          if (nameExists) {
            throw new Error(`An item named "${child.name}" already exists in the destination`);
          }
        }

        // Move each item via SDK (lines 291-301) — LOOPS moveItem
        const client = getSdkClient();
        for (const item of items) {
          await client.moveItem(sourceFolder.ipnsName, destFolder.ipnsName, item.id);
          if (item.type === 'folder') {
            const movedFolder = useFolderStore.getState().folders[item.id];
            if (movedFolder) {
              useFolderStore.getState().setFolder({ ...movedFolder, parentId: destParentId });
            }
          }
        }

        setState({ isLoading: false, error: null });
      } catch (err) {
        const error = err instanceof Error ? err.message : 'Failed to move items';
        setState({ isLoading: false, error });
        throw err;
      }
    },
    []
  );
  ```
  - **LOOPS single `moveItem()` calls** — no batch SDK method

